# Export

A download button next to the search field opens a popover offering one or more export formats. CSV and JSON are built in. Add custom formats (e.g. XLSX, PDF) by registering them under `config.exporters`.

## Defaults

```typescript
const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    // ...
    // Omitted entirely → defaults to { csv: {}, json: {} } — both enabled, CSV first.
    exporters: undefined,
    exportChunkSize: 1000
};
```

| Option            | Type                            | Description                                                                                                                                  | Default |
|:------------------|:--------------------------------|:---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:--------|
| `exporters`       | `ExportersConfig<Data> \| false`| Object keyed by exporter id. Key insertion order = popover format order. `false` disables export. Set a key to `false` to disable that format. | `{ csv: {}, json: {} }` |
| `exportChunkSize` | `number`                        | Maximum rows per chunk fetched during a local export.                                                                                         | `1000`  |

## Disabling or trimming

```typescript
exporters: false                            // remove the download button entirely
exporters: { csv: {}, json: false }         // CSV only
exporters: { json: {}, csv: {} }            // JSON listed first in the popover
```

## Built-in CSV settings

[`BuiltinCsvExporterOptions`](/api-reference/index/type-aliases/BuiltinCsvExporterOptions) — every field is optional; the library supplies a settings component, default values and a persistence codec.

The popover lets users tweak these per export; the chosen values persist to localStorage:

| Setting        | Type                              | Default     |
|:---------------|:----------------------------------|:------------|
| `delimiter`    | `',' \| ';' \| 'tab' \| '\|'`     | `','`       |
| `quoteChar`    | `'"' \| "'"`                      | `'"'`       |
| `lineEnding`   | `'\n' \| '\r\n'`                  | `'\n'`      |
| `includeHeader`| `boolean`                         | `true`      |
| `utf8Bom`      | `boolean`                         | `false`     |
| `useRawValues` | `boolean`                         | `false`     |

`useRawValues: true` skips `formatValue` / the message formatter and emits the underlying value (`String(value)`). Useful for re-import pipelines.

## Custom exporters

Register any format. Two execution modes:

- **Local (`run`)** — produces a `Blob` (or `string`/`ArrayBuffer`) in the browser. Rows are pre-fetched across all pages by the time `run` is called.
- **Remote (`buildUrl`)** — returns a URL the browser navigates to. The server does the work.

Provide both to fall back to local when `buildUrl` returns `undefined`.

```typescript
import type { ExporterOptions, ExportRunContext } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable';
import XlsxSettings from './XlsxSettings.svelte';

interface XlsxSettings { freezeHeader: boolean }

const xlsx: ExporterOptions<XlsxSettings, UserData> = {
    extension: 'xlsx',
    mime: 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet',
    defaultSettings: { freezeHeader: true },
    settingsComponent: XlsxSettings,
    async run(ctx, settings) {
        const { default: ExcelJS } = await import('exceljs');
        const workbook = new ExcelJS.Workbook();
        const sheet = workbook.addWorksheet('Users');
        sheet.columns = ctx.columns.map((col) => ({ header: col.label, key: col.key }));
        sheet.addRows(ctx.rows);
        if (settings.freezeHeader) sheet.views = [{ state: 'frozen', ySplit: 1 }];
        return await workbook.xlsx.writeBuffer();
    }
};

const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    // ...
    exporters: { csv: {}, json: {}, xlsx }
};
```

[`ExportRunContext`](/api-reference/index/interfaces/ExportRunContext) hands `run` the pre-fetched rows, the resolved columns (with translated labels), the active config, the message formatter and an `AbortSignal`. For streaming exporters, use `ctx.fetchOnce` + `ctx.baseRequest` + `ctx.chunkSize` to drive your own chunked fetch.

## Remote export

```typescript
const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    // ...
    exporters: {
        csv: false,
        xlsx: {
            extension: 'xlsx',
            mime: 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet',
            buildUrl: (ctx) => {
                const params = new URLSearchParams({
                    sort: JSON.stringify(ctx.baseRequest.orderBy),
                    q: ctx.baseRequest.searchQuery?.searchText ?? ''
                });
                return `/api/users/export.xlsx?${params}`;
            }
        }
    }
};
```

[`ExportBuildUrlContext`](/api-reference/index/interfaces/ExportBuildUrlContext) carries no rows — just the resolved columns, current request (no pagination) and the full config. The browser navigates to the returned URL, so the server is responsible for emitting the file.

## Settings component contract

A custom `settingsComponent` receives [`ExporterSettingsProps`](/api-reference/index/interfaces/ExporterSettingsProps):

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
    import type { ExporterSettingsProps } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable';
    let { settings, onsettingschange }: ExporterSettingsProps<{ freezeHeader: boolean }> = $props();
</script>

<label class='label cursor-pointer gap-2'>
    <span class='label-text'>Freeze header row</span>
    <input
        type='checkbox'
        class='toggle toggle-primary'
        checked={settings.freezeHeader}
        onchange={(e) => onsettingschange({ ...settings, freezeHeader: e.currentTarget.checked })}
    />
</label>
```

Pair with a `settingsCodec` if you want the choice to persist; otherwise the popover resets to `defaultSettings` on next open.

## See also

- [`DaisyUiDataTableExport`](/api-reference/daisyUi/variables/DataTable) — the export popover component, usable standalone.
- [`resolveExportResult`](/api-reference/index/functions/resolveExportResult) — helper that normalises a `run` return value into a downloadable `Blob`.
- [Internationalisation](/docs/guides/i18n) — `messageConfig.export.*` for every label in the popover.
